  "body": "## Independent ADR 0031 I6 design review\n\n**\u8a2d\u8a08PASS\uff1aI6-A\u5b9f\u88c5\u3078\u9032\u884c\u53ef\u80fd\u3002** This reviews #134 at frozen Author HEAD `418ee68046fdfd03a0e84cc840e5d52fce176b81`, tree `476d32923c9be5e3b60e4e17c8828e3646611c43`, independently of its Design Author. New design findings: **Critical 0 / High 0 / Medium 0 / Low 1**. The nonblocking Low finding asks for explicit foreign-policy-handle and forged-principal negative tests; R10 already prohibits both attacks.\n\n[Independent report](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/blob/dc6e663ea90e55210ed5674cae6c332f66a4ac18/docs/implementation/evidence/adr0031-i6/independent/REPORT.md) \u00b7 [R01\u2013R19 matrix](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/blob/dc6e663ea90e55210ed5674cae6c332f66a4ac18/docs/implementation/evidence/adr0031-i6/independent/MATRIX.md) \u00b7 [findings.json](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/blob/dc6e663ea90e55210ed5674cae6c332f66a4ac18/docs/implementation/evidence/adr0031-i6/independent/findings.json) \u00b7 [reproduction and raw evidence](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/tree/dc6e663ea90e55210ed5674cae6c332f66a4ac18/docs/implementation/evidence/adr0031-i6/independent)\n\n### Exact bindings and scope\n\n- Review PR base: `docs/adr0031-i6-boundary-contract-20261022` / **#134**, SHA `418ee68046fdfd03a0e84cc840e5d52fce176b81`.\n- #134 sole parent #133: `f16e5b1713bde9a2f18263a25397c4b450fd5773`, tree `6bfa580baafa9f6a117b7a0b610c4e65cd031b86`.\n- Review publication HEAD: **`dc6e663ea90e55210ed5674cae6c332f66a4ac18`**.\n- Review publication tree: **`3d70218ecf98f751eb550e6a328a21f65069066f`**.\n- New branch: `review/adr0031-i6-design-independent-20261023`; one child commit, 39 review/evidence files only.\n- All original Author entries remain unchanged. No production source, tests, SQL/UDF/fingerprints, Accepted ADR, previous evidence or parent PR is edited. Both packaged Transfer fences remain intact.\n\nLive initial and prepublication rechecks matched the assigned #134 HEAD/tree and #133 parent. Initial all-state duplicate PR search for this base returned none; #134 had zero reviews/comments and successful `offline` and `sqlite-policy` development checks. Its temporary test-merge `3ca6ec4dd2358c0434c7a33ad47095af338b2999` has exact #133/Author parents and the same tree as Author. Full snapshots are retained. These are development checks, not full runtime acceptance.\n\n### Actual newly executed validation\n\nSelected CPython **3.12.14**, actual SQLite **3.53.1**, source ID `2026-05-05 10:34:17 c88b22011a54b4f6fbd149e9f8e4de77658ce58143a1af0e3785e4e6475127e9`. No added/replaced SQLite library.\n\n| Execution | Actual result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Existing I5 admission + I4 SQL pytest | **246 passed**, exit 0; all 246 exact nodes / 738 successful phases reconciled with JUnit/journal/exit |\n| Reviewer-designed A1/B1/C1/D1/normal-stage probes | **5/5**, exit 0; current I5 boundaries reproduced, true second-INSERT SAVEPOINT rollback verified |\n| Existing identity/identification/order/terminal/Source probes | **15/15**, exit 0; existing domain types only |\n| SQL fence / deferred COMMIT diagnostics | **5 fence states + 1 transaction scenario**, exit 0; pending 1/1 rows after failed COMMIT, explicit ROLLBACK restores 0/0 |\n| Probe/evidence lint and format; policy lint; UTF-8/local links/fences/JSON; frozen-input hashes and staged whitespace | Passed, retained receipts |\n\nInitial reviewer fixture errors and writable-cache setup correction are reported separately. No product test failure is hidden or converted to PASS. Focused tests bind to the unchanged Author runtime/test/build inputs; publication evidence changes full sdist inputs, and no new distribution execution is claimed.\n\n### Findings and implementation entry conditions\n\nI5-A1/B1/C1 are **closed at the design-contract level** by R10\u201312/14, R08, and R09 respectively. They remain **open in the product**, reproduced independently here. I5-F1's asymmetric helper also remains in current code, with full-schema mitigation; R16/T19 requires stronger complete expected-state inspection and normal both-missing reopen refusal. G-R1 remains I7 work; I4-E1 remains the full-sdist evidence-scope carryover.\n\n- **I6-A may start** under a separate implementation authorization: require immutable original Parent/time and prefilter endpoint declarations, service-bound local AdmissionContext/current permissions including replay, lease through commit and explicit rollback; preserve both fences/native/full-report FKs and fail closed for unwired calls. Include I6-L1 policy/principal substitution tests before A acceptance; obtain independent frozen A review.\n- **I6-B follows reviewed A**: existing identity codec reused, strict bounded v5 seven-column/report-reference wire and whole-unit planner, no implicit authorization. Independent codec/cap/cycle/terminal review, normal unwired/Transfer refusal retained.\n- **I6-C follows reviewed B**: real Provider originals/declarations, all guarded composition-root/callsite routes, authorized receiver closure and replay; remove namespace-Parent registration assumptions. Isolated sender\u2192wire\u2192receiver evidence and independent route review required; normal Transfer still refused.\n- **I7/I8 and separate integrated retirement** remain mandatory: trusted stored/recovery validation, G-R1, paired fresh restore/Stop, query/Search parity, both distribution forms and honest broad/all-79 reconciliation before any separately authorized joint fence retirement.\n\nUnexecuted: future I6 implementation/T01\u2013T27 suite, normal Transfer end-to-end, full regression/all-79 reconciliation, new wheel/sdist-derived-wheel execution, I7 recovery, I8 Search and actual Provider/catalog operations. Planned vectors and historical #130 results are not current product PASS.\n\nRemaining publication/review blockers: **none**. This Draft PR submits review results only; no merge, release, deployment, parent PR modification or I6 product implementation.\n\n### Verified publication and hosted development checks\n\nDraft PR #141 was re-fetched after creation: open, `draft=true`, exact intended base SHA `418ee68046fdfd03a0e84cc840e5d52fce176b81` and remote HEAD `dc6e663ea90e55210ed5674cae6c332f66a4ac18`. The GitHub commit API independently confirms tree `3d70218ecf98f751eb550e6a328a21f65069066f` and sole Author parent. New test-merge `84ad64692306e4ab7064a4e926229110768302db` has exact Author/review parents and the same review tree.\n\n[Hosted tests run 39888166171, attempt 1](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/actions/runs/39888166171) passed `sqlite-policy` and `offline`. Actual log receipt ZIP verified: 71,594 bytes, SHA-256 `417430316e2a8619988a2780eaa7655c0fcc09659cc580e01bc9afc76ca7653a`, all 21 indexed payload lengths/digests match. Binding matches feature/test-merge/tree/run/attempt. Manifest: `development_checks_passed`, `full_acceptance=false`, 0 executed product pytest IDs, 211 acceptance files unexecuted. Prose, lint/format, capability/schema and policy checks passed; product runtime pytest and installed distribution steps were skipped. Hosted Python 3.12.15 / SQLite 3.53.1 is measured identity, not full product acceptance.\n\nCLI PR creation returned HTTP 401 before submission; the connected GitHub tool successfully created this PR after a duplicate-state check. Subsequent read confirmed existence and bindings; no unresolved publication blocker remains.\n",
